Prior conversation context:

User: A wheel with fine teeth is attached to the end of a spring with constant k and unstretched length l, as shown. For x > l, the wheel slips freely on the surface, but for x < l the teeth mesh with the teeth on the ground so that it cannot slip. The wheel has mass M and radius R. Assume that all the mass of the wheel is in its rim.

(a) The wheel is pulled to $x = l + b$ and released. How close will it come to the wall on its first trip?

Assistant: \boxed{l - \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} b}

User: (b) How far out will it go as it leaves the wall?

Assistant: \boxed{l + \frac{1}{\sqrt{2}} b}
